flyleaf (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * German. The editor draws in German where the desktop asks for German, and
    in English everywhere else, with nothing to choose: it reads the language
    the desktop already knows. A translation whose English has since changed is
    not shown, so a message is either current or plainly in English.
  * Windows and macOS packaging, and on macOS a document opened by
    double-click and a save that lands through the file's own volume.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 09:45:00 -0500

flyleaf (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An About box, from a button at the bar's right end: the icon, the
    version, what the application is, where it comes from, and the name's
    story. Escape, the backdrop or its button closes it.
  * The icon: a bound book with its cover folded back to the flyleaf, in the
    colours of excelano.com/flyleaf, replacing the placeholder.
  * The first version in the Excelano apt repository.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 22:30:00 -0500

flyleaf (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The general editor. Every value is edited by its kind, the four datetime
    shapes told apart, and can be converted to another kind where it reads as
    one; arrays are editable; comments can be edited, added and removed in
    every place TOML allows one; undo and redo; a source pane showing what a
    save would write, with the row being edited highlighted; open, save and
    save as, with a prompt before unsaved changes are lost.
  * A save keeps the byte order mark, the line endings and the absence of a
    final newline the file had, which the parser alone drops. Every valid
    TOML 1.1.0 case of toml-test round-trips byte for byte, except seven the
    parser itself changes; those are named in the tests and filed upstream.
  * The first package. Registers the desktop entry for application/toml.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 19:40:00 -0500
